# PyInstaller
#  This block came from GitHub's Python .gitignore template, whose assumption
#  ("these files are written by a python script from a template") is FALSE for
#  this project. `autodoc.spec` is hand-maintained source — it carries the
#  post-build copy steps, the excludes/hiddenimports lists, and the build-time
#  config guards, and its header comment is required reading before building.
#
#  Because of the bare `*.spec` below, autodoc.spec was silently untracked from
#  the repo's creation until 2026-08-06: the build was unreproducible from a
#  clean clone and nobody could tell, because the file was always present on the
#  one machine that builds. The negation is what fixes it. Do not remove it, and
#  do not "tidy" it into `*.spec` alone.
*.manifest
*.spec
!autodoc.spec

