# Cursor  
#  Cursor is an AI-powered code editor.`.cursorignore` specifies files/directories to 
#  exclude from AI features like autocomplete and code analysis. Recommended for sensitive data
#  refer to https://docs.cursor.com/context/ignore-files
.cursorignore
.cursorindexingignore

# AutoDoc runtime data — never commit user recordings or generated files
models/
sessions/
output/
exports/
# AutoDoc local config. Excluded so each install keeps its own per-machine
# values and an update can never overwrite them; ship config.example.json as the
# documented starting point instead.
#
# This is NOT here to hide the AI server's metering key — that key also has a
# default in config.py, which is committed, deliberately. It is an attribution
# identifier, not a credential. See HANDOFF.md, "The key is in the public repo
# on purpose".
config.json

# BookStack bot token (publish/token.py). Base64'd "<id>:<secret>" — obfuscated,
# not encrypted, so it must never be committed: this repo is public.
bookstack.token

# Local git history backup bundles created during repo cleanup
*.bundle

# Runtime diagnostic log (written beside the exe)
autodoc.log
autodoc_update.log

# Packaged release zips (scripts/make_release.py) — these are attached to
# GitHub Releases, not tracked in the repo itself.
releases/

